  "Does Allah need a son?": ["Quran 2:116: 'wa qalu-ttakhadha-llahu waladan subhanah.' Does He need a son?", "Sometimes", "Only one", "Yes"],
  "Badi' in 2:117 means...": ["Ibn Kathir 2:117: Badi' is one who makes with no pattern before. Meaning?", "Copier", "Builder of houses", "Painter"],
  "What does 'haqqa tilawatihi' mean?": ["Ibn Kathir 2:121: 'yatlunahu haqqa tilawatih.' Meaning?", "Reading it once", "Singing it loudly", "Reciting it fast"],
  "What did Ibn Mas'ud say proper reciting includes?": ["Ibn Kathir 2:121: what did Ibn Mas'ud say reciting it as it deserves includes?", "Only the stories", "Only a nice voice", "Only speed"],
  "Reading the Quran well means living by it too.": "Ibn Kathir 2:121: haqqa tilawatih means following the Book, not reading alone.",
  "What did Ibrahim ask for his children?": ["Quran 2:124: 'qala wa min dhurriyyati.' What did Ibrahim ask?", "That they be rich", "That they live long", "That they be kings"],
  "Whom does Allah's promise not reach, in 2:124?": ["Quran 2:124: 'la yanalu 'ahdi-z-zalimin.' Not for whom?", "Travelers", "The poor", "The young"],
  "What did Allah make the House, in 2:125?": ["Quran 2:125: 'mathabatan li-n-nasi wa amna.' The House is?", "A fort for war", "A market", "A palace"],
  "Whose wish matched the ayah about Maqam Ibrahim?": ["Bukhari 402: 'I agreed with my Lord in three' and 'wa-ttakhidhu min maqami Ibrahima musalla' came down. Whose words?", "Abu Lahab", "Qarun", "Abu Jahl"],
  "Who were told to purify the House for worshippers?": ["Quran 2:125: 'wa 'ahidna ila Ibrahima wa Isma'ila an tahhira bayti.' Who were told?", "Musa and Harun", "Dawud and Sulayman", "Yunus and Ayyub"],
  "What did Ibrahim ask for Makkah, in 2:126?": ["Quran 2:126: 'rabbi-j'al hadha baladan aminan wa-rzuq ahlahu mina-th-thamarat.' His ask?", "Tall towers", "A big army", "Rivers of gold"],
  "Did Ibrahim's dua come true?": ["Ibn Kathir 2:126: the haram where blood is not shed and fruit is brought. Was the dua answered?", "No", "Only for a day", "Nobody knows"],
  "What does 2:126 teach us to do?": ["Quran 2:126: Ibrahim's 'rabbi-j'al hadha baladan aminan.' The lesson for us?", "Never ask Allah", "Only ask for ourselves", "Give up hope"],
  "Who raised the foundations of the Ka'bah, in 2:127?": ["Quran 2:127: 'yarfa'u ... al-qawa'ida mina-l-bayti wa...' who?", "Adam alone", "Nuh and his son", "Musa and Harun"],
  "What did they pray while working?": ["Quran 2:127: 'rabbana taqabbal minna innaka anta-s-sami'u-l-'alim.' Their dua?", "Pay us well", "Let us rest", "Make us famous"],
  "After a good deed, what does their dua teach?": ["Ibn Kathir 2:127: building the House, yet fearing it may not be accepted. The lesson?", "Boast about it", "Forget Allah", "Ask for praise"],
  "What did they ask for their children, in 2:128?": ["Quran 2:128: 'wa min dhurriyyatina ummatan muslimatan lak.' For their children?", "Riches", "Victory over Makkah", "Many children"],
  "What does 'manasik' mean in 2:128?": ["Quran 2:128: 'wa arina manasikana.' Manasik are?", "Songs", "Markets", "Houses"],
  "Even prophets asked Allah to accept their repentance.": "Quran 2:128: 'wa tub 'alayna,' Ibrahim and Isma'il asked Allah to accept their repentance.",
  "Who answered Ibrahim's dua in 2:129?": ["Ibn Kathir 2:129: 'ana da'watu abi Ibrahim.' Who is that answered dua?", "Musa", "Sulayman", "Yusuf"],
  "What would the messenger do, in 2:129?": ["Quran 2:129: 'yatlu 'alayhim ayatika wa yu'allimuhumu-l-kitaba ... wa yuzakkihim.' His three tasks?", "Collect taxes", "Build palaces", "Lead wars only"],
  "A dua can be answered long after it is made.": "Ibn Kathir 2:129: Ibrahim's dua for a messenger was answered with the Prophet ﷺ ages later.",
  "Who turns away from Ibrahim's way, in 2:130?": ["Quran 2:130: 'illa man safiha nafsah.' Who turns from Ibrahim's millah?", "A wise person", "A scholar", "A prophet"],
  "What was at the heart of Ibrahim's way?": ["Ibn Kathir 2:130: Ibrahim broke from his people's idols. His millah centres on?", "Kings", "Idols", "Stars"],
  "Where is Ibrahim in the Hereafter, in 2:130?": ["Quran 2:130: 'wa innahu fi-l-akhirati la-mina-s-salihin.' Where is he?", "Among the losers", "Unknown", "Forgotten"],
  "What did Ya'qub ask his sons at death, in 2:133?": ["Quran 2:133: 'idh qala li-banihi ma ta'buduna min ba'di?' His question?", "Where will you live?", "What will you eat?", "Who gets my money?"],
  "What did they answer?": ["Quran 2:133: 'na'budu ilahaka ... ilahan wahida.' Their answer?", "Nothing", "Our money", "The stars"],
  "What does this teach parents?": ["Ibn Kathir 2:133: Ya'qub's last wasiyyah was tawhid. The lesson for parents?", "Only leave wealth", "Never talk about faith", "Only care for grades"],
  "Does a good ancestor save you without your own deeds?": ["Quran 2:134: 'laha ma kasabat wa lakum ma kasabtum.' Saved by ancestors?", "Only on Fridays", "Yes, always", "Yes, if famous"],
  "Will you be asked about others' deeds, in 2:134?": ["Quran 2:134: 'wa la tus'aluna 'amma kanu ya'malun.' Asked about whose deeds?", "Only your parents'", "Only your friends'", "Yes, everyone's"],
  "Honor righteous ancestors by doing good like them.": "Ibn Kathir 2:134: a past nation's deeds are theirs, so follow their good and do not rely on their lineage.",
  "Which prophets do Muslims believe in, in 2:136?": ["Quran 2:136: 'la nufarriqu bayna ahadin minhum.' Which prophets?", "Only Musa", "Only Ibrahim", "Only Muhammad ﷺ"],
  "Which of these is named in 2:136?": ["Quran 2:136: 'wa ma utiya Musa wa...' which other prophet is named?", "Khidr", "Luqman", "Dhul-Qarnayn"],
  "Believing in one prophet and rejecting another is fine.": "Quran 2:136 allows a Muslim to distinguish between the prophets, believing in some and rejecting others.",
  "What does 'sibghah' literally mean?": ["Quran 2:138: 'sibghata-llah.' In Arabic, sibghah is literally what?", "A sword", "A song", "A house"],
  "What is 'the sibghah of Allah', says Ibn Abbas?": ["Ibn Kathir 2:138: 'wa man ahsanu mina-llahi sibghah.' Ibn Abbas: sibghah is?", "A painting", "A rainbow", "A flag"],
  "Like dye, faith should show in all our life.": "Ibn Kathir 2:138: sibghat Allah is His din, which colours the whole life of the believer.",
  "What did foolish people question, in 2:142?": ["Quran 2:142: 'ma wallahum 'an qiblatihimu-llati kanu 'alayha?' What did they question?", "The fasting", "The adhan", "The Friday sermon"],
  "What is the answer in 2:142?": ["Quran 2:142: 'qul lillahi-l-mashriqu wal-maghrib.' The answer?", "We got lost", "The old one broke", "It was a mistake"],
  "Which way did the Muslims face before the Ka'bah?": ["Bukhari 40: for sixteen or seventeen months, the Muslims faced which qiblah?", "Egypt", "Persia", "Yemen"],
  "What does 'wasat' mean in 2:143?": ["Bukhari 4487: 'al-wasat al-'adl.' What does wasat mean?", "Lazy", "Late", "Small"],
  "For which prophet will this ummah testify?": ["Bukhari 4487: 'hal ballaghta?' asked of which prophet, with this Ummah as witness?", "Haman", "Fir'awn", "Qarun"],
  "What is a balanced ummah like?": ["Ibn Kathir 2:143: 'ummatan wasata.' A balanced Ummah is?", "Harsh to everyone", "Careless about religion", "Always in the middle of fights"],
